    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-13T10:58:29+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T10:58:29+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-13T00:28:29Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T00:28:29Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough located near the northern border of SA will shift north over the next few days as a high pressure system moves across the south. The high will move into the Tasman Sea later on Thursday with a trough moving into the far west on Friday before weakening over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Oodnadatta, becoming less likely in the late afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the late morning and afternoon. Winds south to southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 20 to 28.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Leigh Creek in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek from the late morning. Winds southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far northeast. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Oodnadatta in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending south to southeasterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 31.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
